.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Gradients and dash patterns, registered once and used by handle\&. 

\fBPart of the host facing interface\&.\fP A host binds to \fBschultz_api\&.h\fP, which includes this header\&. A style value is a small union: a colour, a number, a font\&. A gradient's colour stops and a dash pattern's lengths are both too much to fit in one, and both are usually shared between many nodes, so they are registered here and referred to by handle, exactly as fonts and styles are\&.
.PP
The table sits beside the font system rather than inside the tree because the renderer has to read it, and a renderer that knows about the widget tree would be a renderer coupled to it\&. 
.PP
Definition in file \fBschultz_resource\&.h\fP\&.
